{%- comment -%}
  BMP-MANIFEST (never rendered — grep-able contract for humans and tooling)

  bmp_version: 2.0.0 (config/settings_schema.json theme_info: BuildMyPOD 2.0.0)
  horizon_base: 4.1.4

  This file is one whole-file Liquid comment and renders NOTHING. It is
  rendered from snippets/bmp-globals.liquid purely so theme check's
  OrphanedSnippet stays quiet — only inert whitespace lands in the output.
  Because the repo's docs and markdown files are shopify-ignored,
  this manifest is the only contract artifact that travels with the deployed
  theme. Register of record: the repo's internal upstream-diff register (not
  shipped) — one row per modified
  core file; this index mirrors its hook-name column. Keep the two in sync.

  hooks (every core .liquid file BMP touches, by hook name; names bind to the
  greppable BMP-HOOK markers — adding one requires a register row):
    - layout/theme.liquid#globals              [renders bmp-globals —
        LOAD-BEARING: the whole BMP layer (bmp-styles.css with the visual-
        parity rules, the aria shim, the manifest) loads only because of
        this render line; losing it in an upstream merge fails silently;
        tools/visual-regression.mjs exists to catch exactly that]
    - layout/theme.liquid#body                 [renders bmp-body — the empty
        end-of-body widget slot]
    - layout/theme.liquid#platform-body + #platform-layout    [body class
        buildmypodai-theme + data-buildmypodai-layout="theme"; frozen API]
    - layout/password.liquid#platform-body + #platform-layout [body class
        buildmypodai-theme + data-buildmypodai-layout="password"; frozen API]
    - snippets/cart-drawer.liquid#cart-drawer-progress  [renders
        bmp-free-shipping-bar at the top of the drawer content, inside the
        cart-items-component subtree so cart morphs re-render it]
    - snippets/cart-drawer.liquid#cart-drawer-announcements [renders
        bmp-cart-announcements at the bottom of the cart drawer]
    - snippets/cart-drawer.liquid#cart-drawer-script [script_only
        render next to the cart-drawer.js loader — kept OUTSIDE the morphed
        subtree because section-rendering morphs never re-execute scripts]
    - snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid#pdp-option-value [option legends show
        colon + selected value for every option style ("Size: M"); the legend
        also renders bmp-size-guide-trigger — the in-row size-guide link]
    - snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid#size-required-unselected [the
        RENDER half of forced size selection. Gated on the
        bmp_size_required checkbox (default ON) AND the option name matching
        bmp_size_guide_option (default 'Size') AND the option having MORE THAN
        ONE value: the size option renders with no checked radio
        (data-current-checked="false" kept — core reads that attribute) and, in
        dropdown style, a value="" selected disabled placeholder. Marks the
        gated fieldset data-bmp-size-fieldset="true" for the module's focus and
        outline target. Native pre-selection lines are WRAPPED, never deleted.
        The values.size > 1 condition is load-bearing: a single-value size
        option offers nothing to choose, so gating it would leave Layer 2's
        `disabled` on the hidden input forever. No `required` on the <select>
        on purpose — it would fail form.checkValidity() and show the browser's
        native validation bubble instead of the designed presentation, which is
        how v1.1.5's own guard was bypassed. Gate:
        scripts/check-size-required.mjs]
    - snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid#swatch-name-fallback [marks configured
        Color/Colour options swatch-capable without native linked swatch data and
        passes option/value names to the shared renderer]
    - snippets/swatch.liquid#swatch-name-fallback [override-mode probe ranked
        between native swatch.image and swatch.color, then the final
        full-map fallback after every native branch; resolves validated
        backgrounds through bmp-swatch-color-map and preserves
        swatch--unavailable when blank]
    - snippets/variant-swatches.liquid#swatch-name-fallback [product-card option
        eligibility plus option/value arguments for the shared renderer]
    - blocks/swatches.liquid#swatch-name-fallback [prevents the product-card
        swatches block self-hiding when only name-based fallback data exists]
    - snippets/quick-add.liquid#swatch-name-fallback [keeps single-option card
        Add-vs-Choose behavior aligned with fallback swatch eligibility]
    - blocks/buy-buttons.liquid#size-required-gate + #size-required-layer2
        [captures bmp-size-required-state into
        bmp_size_state (''/open/closed); marks <product-form-component> with
        data-bmp-size-required + data-bmp-size-satisfied, carries the
        data-bmp-size-option / pipe-joined data-bmp-size-values payload the
        module matches app-rendered controls against (moved here from the
        retired message element), and feeds the prompt string into the
        cascade as --bmp-size-required-prompt (core
        add-to-cart-button.liquid:50 emits its label as a bare TEXT NODE, so
        CSS content: fed by an inheriting property is the only label swap that
        touches no further core file and rewrites no textContent — the
        cta-prompt in bmp-styles.css consumes it on a refused interaction —
        data-bmp-size-missing, per the coach decision of 2026-08-18, with the
        shake replayed per blocked click); and stamps `disabled` on the hidden input[name="id"]
        while the gate is shut - Layer 2, the no-JS floor, so a blocked or
        broken script yields NO line item rather than a wrong one. Gate:
        scripts/check-size-required.mjs]
    - blocks/accelerated-checkout.liquid#size-required-express [extends
        the native `unless can_add_to_cart` hidden condition to the
        forced-size gate. The block renders Shopify's own form_obj |
        payment_button, which posts through Shopify's script and not through
        handleSubmit, so Layer 1 cannot intercept it - hiding is the only
        reliable control (D1). The added branch is guarded by
        `can_add_to_cart and ...` so a variant that is both sold out and
        unchosen never emits `hidden` twice on one element. Gate:
        scripts/check-size-required.mjs]
    - sections/header.liquid#org-sameas [renders bmp-org-sameas inside the core
        Organization JSON-LD object, immediately before the native "url" key;
        injects a "sameAs" array built from settings.bmp_seo_social_profiles
        (one absolute URL per line); emits nothing when unset, so the core
        object stays byte-equivalent to stock. Phase-6 opt-in, approved
        2026-08-03]
    - snippets/section.liquid#device-visibility [binds bmp_device_visibility to
        the bmp-hide-on-mobile/desktop classes; this core file carries zero
        CSS — the utility rules live in the overrides layer]
    - blocks/filters.liquid#facets-bar-labels    [gated on bmp_show_bar_labels,
        default off: "Filter:" bar label, "N products" count copy (desktop +
        mobile), mobile "Filter and sort" toggle copy, passes bmp_bar_labels
        to the desktop sorting render]
    - blocks/_slide.liquid#hero-mobile-image     [gated on bmp_image_1_mobile
        (additive schema entry, BMP-SCHEMA:hero-mobile-image): renders the
        desktop crop with hidden--mobile and the mobile crop with
        hidden--desktop at the native 750px breakpoint; unset = stock render]
    - snippets/sorting.liquid#facets-bar-labels  [optional bmp_bar_labels param:
        "Sort by:" summary label + selected value visible on desktop]
    - snippets/header-drawer.liquid#brand-menu-icon [open-state icon swap to
        bmp-icon-menu.svg — the brand three-line hamburger; the artwork lives
        in its own bmp- asset so upstream can never silently overwrite it]
    - snippets/card-gallery.liquid#product-labels
    - snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid#pdp-gallery-arrows
        [with bottom-thumbnail pagination, slide arrows render inside the
        controls row instead of overlaying the main image]
    - snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid#perf-gallery-lazy [the four
        media render sites pass lazy loading for non-first gallery media]
    - snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid#product-labels [first
        child of the <media-gallery> wrapper, so the overlay covers both the
        grid and carousel presentations it renders]
    - snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid#gallery-variant-scope
        [gated on bmp_scope_media_to_variant (additive schema entry,
        BMP-SCHEMA:gallery-variant-scope on blocks/_product-media-gallery
        .liquid), default off = stock: rebuilds sorted_media as the selected
        variant's MEDIA GROUP — its attached image plus every following
        unassigned image, to the next variant-attached one — with non-image
        media appended after it, and re-derives slideshow_controls_style /
        slideshow_class / render_slideshow_arrows / render_controls_arrows
        from the SCOPED count (stock computes them off the unscoped
