        from the bmp_truncate_setting alias — block bmp_truncate_lines with
        bmp_use_global_style off, global bmp_card_title_truncate_lines with it
        on (additive schema entry, BMP-SCHEMA:title-truncate in the same
        file, since 2026-08-17 in the COUNTERPART mirror) — and passes it through
        snippets/text.liquid's own `class` param onto the text-block wrapper;
        '' at none/blank, which text.liquid interpolates exactly like an absent
        param, so the default render is byte-identical to stock. The clamp
        itself is the "Product title truncate" group in
        assets/bmp-styles.css. NOTE: that `class` param has ZERO upstream
        consumers — all 10 core render 'text' sites omit it, on the pinned
        Horizon base and upstream — so a Horizon refactor can drop it as
        dead code and the
        clamp dies silently with CI green. Gate:
        scripts/check-title-truncate.mjs, whose A1 pins both the @param
